{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-015-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/LoopPhaseTests.cs","line":602,"method":"BackwardCompat_MissingKey_ReturnsNull_RecordingTree","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/ParsekScenario.cs:7409; drop the IsNullOrEmpty guard -> red. Deleting the guard at Source/Parsek/RecordingTreeRecordCodec.cs:671 -> still green.","what_it_asserts":"A RECORDING node lacking loopAnchorBodyName leaves Recording.LoopAnchorBodyName null after load.","why_weak":"It loads through ParsekScenario.LoadRecordingMetadataForTests, the same call as its ParsekScenario twin. The RecordingTree/RecordingTreeRecordCodec decode site it names is a separate code path and is never executed, so the tree-side missing-key behavior is unguarded.","proposed_action":"Rebuild the node inside a RECORDING_TREE ConfigNode and load via RecordingTree.Load, then assert null; or rename the test to match what it exercises and add the tree-side case.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-015-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/LoopPhaseTests.cs","line":827,"method":"ComputeOverlapCycleLoopUT_UserPeriodWhileEngineDoubled_ProducesWrongPhase","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GhostPlaybackLogic.WarpLoopPolicy.cs:283; remove the MinCycleDuration clamp -> red. Reverting the #443 WatchModeController effective-cadence fix -> still green.","what_it_asserts":"Passing the user period instead of the effective cadence to ComputeOverlapCycleLoopUT yields loopUT=75.","why_weak":"The docstring presents it as a regression guard for the #443 P1 watch-mode defect, but it pins the output of the wrong call; the production call site (WatchModeController.ResolveWatchPlaybackUT) is never exercised, so re-breaking the fix leaves this green.","proposed_action":"Reword the docstring to 'characterization of the helper clamp', and add a behavioral case over the cadence-resolution seam used by ResolveWatchPlaybackUT.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"RecordingTreeRecordCodec","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/RecordingTreeRecordCodec.cs","sut_line":671,"case_kind":"negative","proposed_name":"RecordingTreeCodec_MissingLoopAnchorBodyNameKey_LeavesNull","sketch":"Build a RECORDING_TREE ConfigNode whose RECORDING child has recordingId/loopPlayback/loopAnchorPid but no loopAnchorBodyName; RecordingTree.Load(node); assert the loaded recording's LoopAnchorBodyName is null.","guards":"A codec change that writes an empty string or a default body name for absent loopAnchorBodyName, which would make loop anchor body validation reject a valid anchor.","risk":"recording"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"WatchModeController","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/WatchModeController.cs","sut_line":3488,"case_kind":"state-transition","proposed_name":"ResolveWatchPlaybackUT_CadenceAdjustedLoop_UsesEffectiveCadence","sketch":"Expose or extract the cadence-selection step of ResolveWatchPlaybackUT as an internal pure helper; for userPeriod=1, duration=164, cap=10 assert the interval handed to ComputeOverlapCycleLoopUT equals ComputeEffectiveLaunchCadence (16.4), not 1.","guards":"Re-introduction of the #443 P1 defect where the watched ghost jumps to the wrong loop phase under any cadence-adjusted recording.","risk":"playback"}
